course: dictionary
lesson: 12002
title: Charitable: kind and giving
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Charitable is an adjective, so it describes a person, a thing or an action. Look at the words around it for clues. «The school held a bake sale to raise money for a charitable cause.» Bake sales raise money for good causes, so charitable must have something to do with helping people in need.
explain: «Mia gave some of her pocket money to a charitable group that feeds hungry families.» Giving money or food to help people in need is charitable. Now look at «The park has a charitable trust that pays for its gardens.» A charitable trust belongs to a charity, so here the word means connected with a charity.
explain: The third meaning is about how you judge people. «Dad was charitable and decided Tom had only forgotten, not done it on purpose.» Dad thought the best of Tom instead of the worst. Check by swapping in your meaning: kind and fair to Tom still makes sense.
fact: Charitable means kind and generous in giving money, food or help to people in need.
fact: Charitable can also mean having to do with a charity, as in «a charitable trust».
fact: Charitable can mean kind in judging others, not thinking the worst, as in «a charitable view».
fact: Charitable work, a charitable donation and «to be charitable» are common phrases.
fact: «To be charitable» means to say the kindest thing you can about someone.
exercise: «The school held a bake sale to raise money for a charitable cause.» What does charitable mean here? | *Kind and generous in helping people in need | Very loud and noisy | Closed for the day | Full of sweets
exercise: «Dad was charitable and decided Tom had only forgotten.» What does charitable mean here? | Rich and famous | Angry and ready to shout | *Thinking the best of someone, not the worst | Sleepy and tired
exercise: «The park has a charitable trust that pays for its gardens.» What does charitable mean here? | *Having to do with a charity | Old and worn | Very tall and thin | Covered in paint
test: Which phrase means to say the kindest thing you can about someone? | Charitable trust | *To be charitable | Charitable donation | Charitable work
test: What is a charitable donation? | A map of the local park | A receipt for a new coat | *A gift of money or food to help people in need | A fine for breaking a rule
exam: Which use of charitable means kind in judging others? | *Sam took a charitable view and believed Jo when she said the vase broke by accident | Ben made a charitable donation of his old books | The charity shop sells charitable goods | The charitable trust raised money for a new roof
